It looks like the "travel" algorithm is checking
connectivity, but not including your burden in the
check while planning a path, just checking burden
restrictions move by move as the moves occur, so
that when you get to the cell shown, you can't
squeeze through to the cell northwest of it, so
travel recomputes your path, moves you right
instead, temporarily disqualifying that
northwestward path. Now, though, your old path has
been invalidated, and travel must recompute a new
one.

When travel recomputes your path, the path left and
then northwest still looks shortest, burden no
longer being considered, so you get moved left, but
cannot squeeze through to the northwest on the next
move.

Lather, rinse, repeat.

That's definitely a bug, though that's only a guess
at how it occurs, and your map should be passed
along to the Dev Team.

